load @term/seed/group
  find group

# An abelian group: a group whose operation commutes, so a times b equals b times a for every pair. The order of
# composition stops mattering. The integers under addition are the first abelian group, and every vector space is an
# abelian group under its addition. Commutativity is the law the quaternions lose at the fourth rung of the tower and
# the complex numbers still keep, so the additive structure stays abelian all the way up while the multiplicative
# structure need not. The form carries the underlying group; the commutativity law is the extra axiom an instance
# satisfies.
form abelian-group
  link group, like group
